          <h1>Guidelines</h1>
            > Logic gets its name from the Greek word logos, which has two meanings, for logos means “word” and “reason”. Whence logic is divided into a rational and a discursive science. Rational logic, which is called argumentative, comprises dialectic and rhetoric. Discursive logic is the genus to which grammar, dialectic, and rhetoric belong, and it thus comprises the argumentative.
                 — Hugh of Saint Victor

